accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  correctedtype  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  accessioned on  18 removed_month 97 at 12 49 clinical data   none provided      revised report     reason for revision  additional outside slides received revised by  frederick carl koerner  m d  revised on 10 removed_month 97 at 11 43                                                                                     final diagnosis     breast  right   excisional biopsy  invasive ductal carcinoma  grade 2  extending to the margin of the specimen along a broad front  ductal carcinoma in situ  confined to the mass  lobular neoplasia  see note  note  blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  diagnosis by  frederick carl koerner  m d  edited by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  10 removed_month 97 at 13 49                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  right   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  10 removed_month 97 at 13 49                                                                                 source care unit  mgh outside location reports to  barbara lynn smith  m d  simon powell  m d  michael l grossbard  m d  outside institution  the cambridge hospital outside pathologist  john p  grabbe  m d  pathology dept   cambridge hospital  removed_case_id  cambridge street cambridge  ma  removed_case_id  part   right breast biopsy  97  removed_accession_id   date of procedure  22 jan  removed_case_id  slides  2 blocks  1 , No.
