y contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  11 removed_month 96 at 07 26     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     this addendum has been deleted for this report gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a removed_date x removed_date x 1 0cm fragment of breast with a removed_date x removed_date x 0 7cm firm to hard mass within less than 0 1cm of surface ink  representative sections of mass frozen as fx 1  resubmitted in a  remainder in b j  resident  edwin s  monuki  md     intra operative diagnosis     frozen section diagnosis  1  right breast  infiltrating ductal carcinoma  o r  resident  maryam s  mohammadkhani  md o r  diagnosis by  ben zion pilch  m d                                                                                  source care unit  same day surgical unit    removed_accession_id  reports to  peter hedberg  m d  wiley w souba jr   m d  part   right breast biopsy   report_end  , No.
